// handler-sidecar <-> task-grid node.
//
// The sidecar runs next to a handler and connects to the node; the node sends it attempts of the handler's kind.
// Payloads and results are bytes: their types are known only to whoever submits the task and to the handler.
//
// Slots belong to the sidecar (credits). The node sends attempts only while it holds credit of the session:
// - the node tells its demand - how many attempts it would like to send to this sidecar (Demand);
// - the sidecar grants slots as credit (Credit); unused credit plus attempts in progress never exceed its capacity.
// Credit and demand are absolute values (limit / target with a version), not increments: a lost or repeated
// message breaks nothing, and the node returns surplus credit with the same Demand.
//
// A session is one Connect stream. A new session of the same worker_id supersedes the previous one (its stream
// is closed with OK). When a session breaks (cancellation, error), its attempts in progress are retried by the node:
// a result sent for them later is accepted and ignored.
//
// Shutdown of the sidecar (drain): stop granting credit and half-close the stream. The node sends no more attempts,
// waits for the results of the attempts in progress (Complete) and then closes the stream with OK.

